!.env.example
# The per-market template. The root `.gitignore` already un-ignores it, and
# that was not enough: a nested `.gitignore` wins for the files beneath it, so
# `.env.*` here quietly re-ignored the one file the runbook tells an operator
# to copy on the server. It was untracked for a week and nobody could see it,
# because an ignored file does not appear in `git status`.
!.env.example.market
